<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ADAPTIVE ICON, API 26 and up.

  WHY THIS FILE IS NOT CALLED appicon.xml
  =======================================
  Resizetizer generates mipmap-anydpi-v26/appicon.xml from the MauiIcon Include's
  basename, and hard-codes the monochrome layer to the full-colour foreground raster:

    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/appicon_foreground" />

  MonochromeFile is a .NET MAUI 11 property and does not exist in 10.0.101, so the only
  way to supply a real monochrome layer is a project resource. A project resource that
  used the name "appicon" would land in the app's own res directory
  (MonoAndroidResDirIntermediate, which aapt2 link receives as a primary overlay via -R)
  while the generated file arrives as a LibraryResourceDirectory (aapt2's library-path
  argument). That pairing is resolved as an overlay rather than a duplicate, but it depends
  on aapt2's precedence rules holding for this toolchain, and the generated name is derived
  from the MauiIcon Include - rename the Include, or add a second MauiIcon, and the
  override silently stops matching.

  So the name is deliberately different: "cafepos_icon" is a name Resizetizer cannot
  generate. It is derived from the MauiIcon basename ("appicon") plus "_round", never
  from a project file name, so there is nothing for it to collide with under any
  precedence rule. AndroidManifest.xml points android:icon and android:roundIcon here.

  WHY THE LAYERS ARE WHAT THEY ARE
  ===============================
  background  @mipmap/appicon_background - the raster Resizetizer produces from
              Resources/AppIcon/appicon.svg, which is now a flat #143D59 fill and nothing
              else. Using the generated raster keeps the MauiIcon Color attribute the one
              place the background colour is declared.
  foreground  @drawable/cafepos_mark - vector, 108x108 viewport, geometry documented
              there. Preferable to the generated PNG foreground: the themed layer below
              is a vector, and having the colour layer as one too means the two can be
              diffed.
  monochrome  @drawable/cafepos_icon_monochrome - the actual fix. Themed icons are
              required from API 33, and from Android 16 QPR2 the system auto-themes apps
              that have no monochrome layer, which with targetSdkVersion=36 happens
              whether or not the operator opts in. That tag is only parsed on API 33+,
              which is also why cafepos_icon_monochrome.xml can rely on being a vector
              without worrying about API 21-32.

  No separate round variant: the launcher applies its own circular crop, which is what
  android:roundIcon is for. The generated mipmap/appicon_round.png is a byte-for-byte copy
  of mipmap/appicon.png, so pointing roundIcon at it bought nothing.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/appicon_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/cafepos_mark" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@drawable/cafepos_icon_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
